# Vendored third-party build outputs are stored byte-for-byte.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf normalization rewrites their line endings on
# checkout, which changes their SHA-256 and makes the checksums recorded in
# src/ui/vendor/README.md fail to verify. They are never edited here, so there
# is nothing to gain from normalizing them.
src/ui/vendor/*.js -text
